WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Her name was Jo Ann Morris [Evelyn’s sister-in-law].

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:16.020
They met and decided that they would go and sit in at the Woolworth store in Baton Rouge on Third Street.

3
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.300
And they were arrested.

4
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:28.160
It was fourteen of them between a couple of places that they were sitting in.

5
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.420
She was arrested.

6
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.620
But not only was she arrested,

7
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:51.620
the governor at the time (I think it was the governor) decided that everybody who had participated in that sit-in would be expelled or dismissed from Southern [University].

8
00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.500
She was a freshman and she was dismissed from Southern.

9
00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.640
And they could not attend any university in the state of Louisiana.

10
00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.440
Any public university in the state of Louisiana.

11
00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:19.080
She ended up having to go to Central State University in Ohio, I think it is, because of her participation in the civil rights movement.
